  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dangerous heat continues today closer to the coast. \n\nAlthough increasing showers/storms/clouds will keep temperatures and \nheat indices lower in some spots we will keep the Heat Advisory up \nfor at least a few more hours for heat indices generally in the 105-\n109 degree range.   \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Isolated severe storms and flash flooding possible \ninto tonight, with a low risk for flash flooding continuing on \nSaturday.\n\nA trough in the jet stream and attendant cold front progressing \neastward into the Carolinas will yield scattered to numerous showers \nand thunderstorms into this evening. A Severe Thunderstorm Watch has \nrecently been issued for mainly the risk of damaging wind gusts, \nalthough large hail and a tornado can't completely be ruled out. \nModerate to strong instability, steep low-level lapse rates, and \nanomalously high precipitable water values (~2\"+) will all \ncontributing to a wet microburst threat. Frequent lightning and very \nheavy rainfall are also expected with isolated flash flooding \npossible, especially inland from the coast where storms move over \nthe same areas for an extended period. A low flood risk will \ncontinue into Saturday, mainly near/east of I-95 and in areas that \npick up a good deal of rain today/tonight. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...Near-normal temperatures expected starting this \nweekend with low rain chances Sunday/Monday before increasing mid \nweek.\n\nScattered showers and thunderstorms will remain possible through \nSaturday night as a cold front stalls just west of or over the \nforecast area while impulses aloft continue to move through the \nbroader trough in the jet stream. A period of mostly dry weather \nappears likely on Sunday and Monday as the front is shoved offshore. \nHowever, as the flow aloft becomes westerly to northwesterly around \nmidweek, additional impulses and waves of low pressure are poised to \nbring periods of showers and thunderstorms from Tuesday onward, with \nthe best chances for more widespread rain currently focused on \nThursday. Of course, given this is multiple days away, the chances \nfor rain will likely fluctuate in the coming days as smaller-scale \ndetails are worked out.",
